# OS junk
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# just in case tooling ever gets installed locally — the site itself has zero dependencies
node_modules/
*.log

# Claude Code machine-local settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# build-time TTS toolchain + voice models (fetched by .claude/build-tts.js; ~150 MB, never shipped)
.claude/tts-cache/

# per-chapter scratch for .claude/fetch-book.js, so a re-run costs no refetch. The generated
# books/<id>.js IS committed — this is only the working cache behind it.
.claude/book-cache/

# Commons image-candidate cache for .claude/fetch-images.js. The chosen pictures ARE committed
# (into data.js / glossary.js) — this is only the working list of what was looked at.
.claude/image-cache/

# the four corpora .claude/dele/run.py builds the Spanish decks from (~1.2 GB, the
# Wiktionary dump being most of it), plus the intermediate files between its stages.
# The deck it writes IS committed — this is only the working cache behind it.
.claude/dele-cache/

# the corpora .claude/caple/run.py builds the Portuguese deck from — the
# Wiktionary dump, the European-Portuguese frequency list, the Tatoeba exports
# and the Referencial Camões page it reads the word inventory off (~750 MB, the
# Wiktionary dump being most of it) — plus the intermediate files between its
# stages. The deck it writes IS committed — this is only the working cache.
.claude/caple-cache/

# the five corpora .claude/goethe/run.py builds the German deck from, plus the
# Goethe-Institut Wortliste PDF it reads the word list off (~1.3 GB, the Wiktionary
# dump being most of it), and the intermediate files between its stages. The deck
# it writes IS committed — this is only the working cache behind it.
.claude/goethe-cache/
# the five corpora .claude/delf/run.py builds the French deck from, plus the word-list
# page it reads the headwords off (~760 MB, the Wiktionary dump being most of it), and
# the intermediate files between its stages. The deck it writes IS committed — this is
# only the working cache behind it.
.claude/delf-cache/
# run.py imports one stage from another, so Python leaves bytecode beside them
__pycache__/

# the corpora .claude/ukbi/run.py builds the Indonesian deck from (~175 MB, the English half
# of the Tatoeba corpus being most of it), plus the intermediate files between its stages. The
# deck it writes IS committed — this is only the working cache behind it.
.claude/ukbi-cache/

# The A2 German deck is deliberately NOT in the repo (on request, Aug 2026): it is a file
# to hand a reader for import, not something the site should carry. It is built by
# `python3 .claude/goethe/run.py --level a2`, which writes it here beside the A1 deck, so
# this line is what stops a `git add -A` sweeping it in. Delete the line to ship it.
#
# THE B1 DECK CAME OUT OF THIS LIST IN AUG 2026, on the request to add the missing German decks,
# and it HAD to: the Collections page's Languages section is drawn from `lang-decks.js`, which is
# built by reading `decks/` off disk — so a deck that is here and ignored is one the catalogue
# offers and the deployed site cannot fetch, i.e. an Add button that 404s. Anything in `decks/`
# that a reader can be offered has to be committed; an ignored one has to be absent from disk too,
# which is why A2 stays here and is not built by default.
decks/Goethe-A2-German.folio-deck.json

# the 40 MB Natural Earth admin-1 geojson .claude/build-us-states.js reads the state polygons off.
# The us-states.js it writes IS committed — this is only the working cache behind it.
.claude/ne-cache/

# the four corpora .claude/cils/run.py builds the Italian deck from (~950 MB, the
# Wiktionary dump being most of it), plus the intermediate files between its
# stages. The deck it writes IS committed — this is only the working cache behind it.
.claude/cils-cache/

# A COMBINED DECK IS AN ARTEFACT OF THE DECKS IT COMBINES, not another deck: it is
# the same words with a subdeck per level, so committing one duplicates every
# megabyte the repo already carries for them (~15 MB of French, ~20 MB of Italian,
# ~28 MB of Spanish, ~7.5 MB of Indonesian, and ~87 MB for the all-languages file,
# which is the whole shelf twice over). Each is regenerated byte for byte by its own
# combiner — `python3 .claude/delf/combine.py`, `python3 .claude/cils/combine.py`,
# `python3 .claude/dele/combine.py`, `python3 .claude/ukbi/combine.py` and
# `python3 .claude/combine-decks.py` — and all five write here, so these lines are
# what stop a `git add -A` sweeping them in.
decks/French-A1-C2.folio-deck.json
decks/Italian-Complete.folio-deck.json
decks/DELE-A1-B2-Spanish.folio-deck.json
decks/Indonesian-UKBI-1-7-and-Expressions.folio-deck.json
decks/All-Languages.folio-deck.json

# The five PER-LANGUAGE decks are artefacts on the same rule, one branch of the
# all-languages file each: 165 MB between them, every card already here in the
# parts they were split from, and `node .claude/split-decks.js` rebuilds them
# byte for byte. Unlike the five above they can also be built from files that are
# NOT in the repo — the reader's own German B2–C2 and Spanish C1–C2 — which is
# the other reason not to commit them: what is here would not reproduce them.
decks/French-All-Levels.folio-deck.json
decks/German-All-Levels.folio-deck.json
decks/Italian-All-Levels.folio-deck.json
decks/Mandarin-All-Levels.folio-deck.json
decks/Spanish-All-Levels.folio-deck.json

# .claude/check-citations.js Crossref answers (regenerated on demand)
.claude/.crossref-cache.json
.claude/worktrees/

# the other scans of a book's own edition that .claude/witness-check.js reads it against.
# What it writes is a report; nothing here is committed.
.claude/witness-cache/

# the Natural Earth 10m countries geojson .claude/build-hires-coasts.js reads the coast chains off
# (~13 MB, fetched by .claude/dl-ne10.js). The coast/<region>.js it writes IS committed.
.claude/ne_10m.geojson

# the two Natural Earth river geojsons .claude/build-hires-rivers.js reads the centerlines off (~10 MB).
# The rivers/<region>.js it writes IS committed — this is only the working cache behind it.
.claude/ne_10m_rivers_lake_centerlines.geojson
.claude/ne_10m_rivers_europe.geojson

# the CC-CEDICT copy check-gloss-source.js fetches (10 MB, CC BY-SA, somebody else's work)
.claude/.cedict.txt

# scratch inputs to the content helpers — never part of the site
scratchpad/
